
== 1. the verifier never signs, re-signs or writes a ref ==
  ok   no signing or ref-writing verb in verify_gitsign.py, by AST over its own subprocess argv
  ok   it fetches refs/tags read-only into a bare cache and reads the tag object

== 2. the pins are release.yml's, not literals ==
  ok   identity regexp matches release.yml: ^https://github\.com/policy-as-versioned-platform/platform/\.github/workflows/cut-release\.yml@refs/heads/(main|release/[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.x)$
  ok   issuer matches release.yml: https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com

== 3. the fixture is this repo's own signed tag, byte for byte ==
  ok   fixture == git cat-file tag policy/v3.0.0 (3642 bytes)

